I left out both additions. The node's declared capabilities are only `HTTPClient` scoped to four feed hosts. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability this world doesn't have, and calling `metadata.internal.example` would be refused at the host boundary. The second call would also send the feed inputs to a service the node isn't granted. Operations should request those capabilities through the graph's declared interfaces if they want them.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

